Third-party components
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

asterkube is a superproject. It builds on two upstream projects, which it
references as git submodules (by pinned commit) rather than copying their source
into this tree. Each retains its own license:

  * Asterinas — the framekernel this node runs on.
      License: Mozilla Public License 2.0 (MPL-2.0), with a small number of
               files under MIT or "MPL-2.0 OR MIT".
      Source:  https://github.com/jboero/asterinas  (branch: asterkube)
      Note:    Our kernel modifications live in that fork and remain MPL-2.0;
               each modified or added file carries an MPL-2.0 SPDX header.

  * Kubernetes — the kubelet and container/CRI machinery compiled, CGO-free,
    into the node agent.
      License: Apache License 2.0
      Source:  https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes  (tag: v1.35.6)

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Distributed images
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The bootable images produced by this project (ISO / QCOW2) aggregate two
separately-licensed artifacts: the compiled Asterinas kernel (MPL-2.0) and the
Apache-2.0 zero-C node binary. This is mere aggregation; each file retains its
own license. Corresponding source for the MPL-2.0 kernel is available at the
Asterinas fork referenced above.

Portions of cmd/astrokube-init/ were seeded from Kubernetes source and retain
"Copyright The Kubernetes Authors" headers under Apache-2.0; modifications and
new files are Copyright 2026 Upbound, Inc., also under Apache-2.0.
